1. **Upright/Transform in the loupe and thumbnails**: the interactive (resident GPU) render path and preview/thumbnail generation must apply the composed geometry (lens + Upright + manual transform + crop) exactly as export does; parity test vs export at L2; slider drag latency stays within the existing budget (log numbers). Guided Upright needs the uncorrected image for guide placement: expose a `render_uncorrected` flag on the session for the Guided overlay.
2. **AI Denoise**: remove the need for a host-supplied per-camera noise setup — estimate the noise profile from the raw (dark-frame-free estimate from flat regions / camera metadata; document the method) so the loupe renders it; export uses the same denoiser (GPU-resident CFA path from M3-16c where available); a model download/progress API on the FFI (listener callbacks: queued, downloading bytes/total, ready, failed with reason; respects an "allow downloads" setting). Tests with fixtures/raw (skip model parts cleanly without weights).
3. **Lens Blur**: produce the depth map on demand with ml-depth for render and export (hook like ai_masks.rs; cached per image+recipe-relevant hash in the preview cache), so recipes containing lens_blur render and export instead of failing; expose `depth_histogram(image_id)` and a `render_depth_visualisation` option on the session; subject-aware focus (ml-segment subject) and focal range; add the remaining bokeh shapes the recipe schema defines. Without weights: a clear error surfaced to the panel (not a failed export of the whole photo — export should skip lens blur with a warning in the report).
Update DevelopEngineGaps consumers? No — do NOT edit Swift; list in the report which gaps are closed so M2-50 can enable the panels. Regenerate bindings; keep `swift build` green.
